            # DECLARED (mir_lowering_types.spl:424-425) but initialised nowhere
            # -- not here, and by no later assignment -- so every MirLowering
            # carried them as `Value::Nil` for the process's whole life. The
            # first `find_global_static` read (expr_dispatch.spl:223,
            # `self.global_statics_by_id.contains(symbol_id)`) was therefore
            # fatal: `method `contains` not found on type `nil``. This aborted
            # the MCP native build inside MIR lowering, not before it. Omitting
            # a Dict field from a constructor call leaves it nil rather than an
            # empty dict, and the desugared receiver shows up in the diagnostic
